	abstract = {This paper proposes a zero-shot Text-to-SQL method based on large language model (LLM) prompt learning, which we call the AMPC-SQL. Specifically, we utilize large models to play two roles: Actor and Critic. The Actor is responsible for generating SQL statements, while the Critic evaluates the correctness of the Actor's generated results. We require the Critic to evaluate from multiple perspectives, hence referring to it as a Multi-Perspective Critic. We conducted experiments using the GPT-3.5 model and the GPT-4o model on the BIRD dataset, achieving significant results. © 2025 IEEE.},
