	affiliations = {Mlr Institute of Technology, Dept of CSE-AIML, Hyderabad, India},
	abstract = {The interfaces of natural language data analytics are trying to avoid relying on structured query languages which inherently restrict the access to the databases to only the technically literate user. The article elaborates on a conversion system through AI of natural language to SQL conversion where dynamically generated data would be viewed to support the textual or voice-recognized query system in many languages. The proposed system takes input in the form of user entries that are represented by normalization, semantic embedding, and similarity search with assistance of a FAISS-based vector cache to utilize the already tested SQL patterns that were successfully tested in the past. A hybrid reasoning approach in case of inappropriate match in which deterministic rule templates are combined with schema-aware big language model orchestration with local and cloud based model is implemented. A process of entity-swapping modifies the SQL queries in accordance with the new purpose of the user by substituting literals and schema items to preserve the accuracy. All queries generated are maintained prior to the implementation on the relational data bases. Visualization with rules has been achieved to do an automatic conversion of query results into structured tables and visualization products.  © 2026 IEEE.},
