	affiliations = {West Ukrainian National University, 11 Lvivska street, Ternopil, 46009, Ukraine},
	abstract = {Natural Language Processing (NLP) is key to enabling intuitive interaction with structured data, especially via natural language interfaces for SQL query generation. However, accurately translating complex user input into executable SQL remains challenging due to ambiguity, schema diversity, and DBMS variability. While prior work has applied transformer-based large language models (LLMs) and Text-toSQL datasets, gaps remain in voice input, multilingual support, and local data privacy. This paper introduces a desktop AI solution that combines transformer architectures, voice recognition, and Ukrainian language support to convert natural language into SQL queries. Built with GPT-4o and PyQt6, the modular system integrates intent classification, named entity recognition, and export features. Testing on 550 queries demonstrated 94% accuracy for text and 91% for voice input, outperforming comparable tools in speed and reliability. Future work will address DBMS integration, system scalability, and context-aware, conversational query refinement for improved Human-AI interaction. © 2025 IEEE.},
