	year = {2025},
	journal = {Proceedings of the International Joint Conference on Neural Networks},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/IJCNN64981.2025.11227969},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105023973772?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Qilu University of Technology, China; Qilu University of Technology, Information Research Institute of Shandong Academy of Sciences, China},
	abstract = {The Text-to-SQL task is to convert natural language queries into Structured Query Language (SQL) to achieve a natural language interface for database queries. The current research on Text-to-SQL primarily focuses on handling complex queries (such as nested queries and multi-table joins), while neglecting those that require complex computations. To address this issue, this paper constructs a Text-to-SQL dataset with a relatively high proportion of computational questions, termed as ESDS, and designs a Text-to-SQL framework based on large language models, named CCS-SQL, to enhance the parsing capability for computational questions. The three core modules of the framework are Schema Linking(SL), Query Classification and Prompting(QCP), and Consistency Calibration Optimization(CCO). SL is responsible for accurately matching the table column names and primary-foreign key relationships involved in the questions;the QCP classifies the questions and designs differentiated prompting strategies; the CCO verifies and optimizes the SQL statements generated by the large language model. Experiments conducted on the ESDS dataset, as well as public datasets, have demonstrated the effectiveness and generalizability of the CCS-SQL framework. © 2025 IEEE.},
