	affiliations = {Indian Institute of Technology, Ieor Department, Mumbai, India; Defence Institute of Advanced Technology, Cse Department, Pune, India},
	abstract = {Osquery is a widely used security monitoring and endpoint visibility platform that exposes system state through a large, fixed schema of more than 100 tables. Threat hunters and security analysts often struggle to use the schema effectively, as it requires translating their investigative intent into precise SQL queries - creating a barrier to fast and efficient threat detection.. To remove this barrier, we propose a domain-specific Natural Language to SQL (NL2SQL) system for Osquery. Our approach constructs a synthetic Osquery-focused dataset, where Large Language Models generate realistic threat-hunting questions paired with accurate SQL queries. Using this dataset, we develop a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline: a retrieval module selects the most relevant Osquery tables for a given natural language input, and a generative model produces the final SQL query conditioned on the retrieved schema. Our strategy showcases the possibilities of integrating retrieval-augmented generation with domain specialization for high accuracy, schema-awareness, and efficiency in NL2SQL conversion for big structured databases. © 2026 IEEE.},
