	affiliations = {Guangdong Power Exchange Center Co., Ltd., Guangdong, Guangzhou, 510000, China},
	abstract = {With the accelerated digital transformation of the power market and the surge in power transaction data, business personnel have an increasingly urgent need for intelligent query tools for Natural Language to SQL (NL2SQL). Current general-purpose NL2SQL models suffer from semantic understanding biases in the power trading field, struggling to identify domain-specific terminology and adapt to business rules, resulting in low SQL generation accuracy and insufficient practicality. This paper first constructs a dataset and knowledge base for the power trading domain. Then, based on Llama 2/ERNIE 4.0, it designs a domain-specific large-scale model fine-tuning strategy to optimize the semantic understanding module. Finally, it implements an end-to-end intelligent NL2SQL question-answering system for power trading. Experimental results show that, in power trading scenarios with small amounts of semantic understanding (≤10,000 records), the response time difference between the two solutions is small: the proposed solution takes approximately 50-120ms, while the unoptimized solution takes approximately 80-180ms, effectively meeting the structured data query needs of business personnel. © 2026 The Authors.},
