	abstract = {This paper proposes a novel end-to-end 5G-A network operation optimization method with three core innovative modules based on multi-source data fusion and intelligent sensing, and verifies it in a provincial-level commercial network. Based on actual operational data of a provincial commercial 5G-A network, the study constructs a multi-source dataset integrating terminal specification information, network access characteristics, performance indicators, and user tags, covering 15 months of operational data, 230 million network event records, and 287,000 user samples from across the province. Firstly, a pre-trained large language model is introduced to construct a novel LLM-driven dynamic data closed-loop mechanism for terminal information calibration; furthermore, based on general natural language to query (Text2SQL) technology and combined with 5G-A domain knowledge, an innovative domain-enhanced intelligent query engine is constructed, supporting semantic understanding of business terms, multi-round interactive queries, and automatic result visualization. Experimental results show that the proposed method increases the collection coverage of key 5G-A network indicators from 0% to 100%; the accuracy of terminal user identification increases from 30% of traditional methods to 95.3%; the intelligent query system reduces the average data acquisition time for frontline personnel from 2 hours to 4.2 minutes, achieves a multi-round query intent understanding accuracy of 91.5%, and generates dynamic reports covering 23 business scenarios. The research results have been widely applied in network operations, supporting related business analysis and efficiency improvement. The study demonstrates that multi-source data fusion and intelligent sensing methods can effectively improve the operational efficiency and user identification capabilities of 5G-A networks, providing valuable practical experience for the intelligent operation of communication networks.  © 2026 