	affiliations = {Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Koneru Lakshmaiah Education Foundation Vaddeswaram, Andhra Pradesh, Vijayawada, India},
	abstract = {The artificial intelligence task of Natural Language to SQL (NL2SQL) conversion empowers non-technical users to query databases using plain language, enhancing data accessibility across sectors such as business intelligence, healthcare, and customer service. However, traditional systems struggle with ambiguity, complex query structures, and schema adaptability, limiting their effectiveness. This study introduces a novel NL2SQL framework that combines advanced preprocessing techniques, a hybrid feature selection approach using Cat Hunting Optimization and War Strategy Optimization, and a Probabilistic Spiking Return-Aligned Decision Transformer Neural Network (PSRANN) for precise SQL generation. Additionally, a Subtraction-Average-Based Optimizer (SABO) is employed to enhance model training efficiency. The proposed framework achieves a remarkable 99.9 % accuracy on the Spider dataset while demonstrating superior performance in precision, recall, F1-score, and query efficiency compared to existing models. The system shows strong adaptability to diverse query structures and database schemas. This work's novelty lies in its biologically inspired neural architecture and dual-optimization strategy, offering a highly accurate, scalable, and robust solution for NL2SQL tasks. Future work will focus on multilingual support, real-time applications, and deployment in domain-specific environments. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.},
