	affiliations = {Harbin Institute of Technology, School of Computer Science, Shenzhen, China; Harbin Institute of Technology Peng Cheng Laboratory, School of Computer Science, Shenzhen, China},
	abstract = {The ever-growing data volume in relational databases and the specialized skills required for writing SQL queries present significant challenges for users attempting to access and analyze data. text-to-SQL offers a solution to these problems. It leverages natural language processing (NLP) techniques to transform natural language into SQL queries. With the advancement of Large Language Models (LLMs), a variety of LLM-based text-to-SQL methods have come into existence. This survey offers a thorough review of the schemes and methods of LLMs based text-to-SQL. We first introduce the fundamental concept and challenges in text-to-SQL, then, we review the dataset, benchmark and evaluation matrix. After that, we present a systematic and comprehensive analysis of recent advances in LLM-based text-to-SQL. Finally, we discuss future directions in this field. © 2025 IEEE.},
